# =========================
# CXOS Platform - Git Ignore
# =========================
# Rule: nothing generated is committed. If a build writes it, it goes here.

# -------------------------
# Signing and Secure Boot key material - NEVER commit any of it.
# .xksk is the platform root: a leaked one lets anyone sign a kernel this
# machine will load. .xusk is a publisher's or a user's. A committed Secure
# Boot PK lets anyone sign a binary that an enrolled machine trusts forever.
# -------------------------
*.xksk
# Only the PLATFORM public key is tracked. Any other pair in tools/ - a local
# test key - is local to one machine: its private half can never be committed,
# so the public half alone would be of no use to anyone else.
tools/*.xkpk
!tools/kernel.xkpk
*.xusk
boot/uefi/sbkeys/
*.pfx
*.pem
*.cer
*.key
*.crt
*.esl
*.auth
*_VARS.fd
*.signed.efi

# -------------------------
# OS build output (CMake)
# -------------------------
/build/
/dist/
/iso/
os/executive/app_image.h
# trusted_key.c is generated into build/ from tools/<key>.xkpk by the build
# itself now, so there is nothing to ignore in the source tree. The .h beside
# it IS tracked: it is two extern declarations and carries no key material.
boot/uefi/BOOTX64.EFI
boot/uefi/*.obj
*.o
*.obj
*.elf
*.bin
*.img
*.iso
*.map
*.d

# The DevKit is not committed as a binary: take `cxk` from a release, or
# publish it from devkit/ (see README).
tools/cxk
tools/cxk.exe

# -------------------------
# .NET build output (devkit/)
# -------------------------
**/bin/
**/obj/
TestResults/
artifacts/
publish/
**/Properties/PublishProfiles/
*.user

# DocFX output: regenerated by `dotnet docfx`
docs/devkit/_site/
docs/devkit/api/

# -------------------------
# Editors, tools, OS noise
# -------------------------
.vs/
.idea/
*.suo
*.code-workspace
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
.cache/
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store
memory_store.json
repomix-output.xml
repomix.config.json
.gitignore

# -------------------------
# Agent / assistant working files. Local only: they are instructions for tools
# the author happens to use, not part of CXOS, and they date faster than the
# code they describe.
# -------------------------
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.repomixignore
repomix-output.*
AGENTS.md
.cursorrules
